+# Proposal
+
+## Why
+
+Customers can create orders and coupons exist in the system, but there is no way to redeem a coupon against a pending order. `CouponService`'s own comment notes that "applying coupons to orders is not implemented yet". Customers need to reduce what they owe by applying one coupon after ordering and before paying.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Add `POST /orders/:id/apply-coupon` accepting `{ "couponCode": "..." }`.
+- Normalize the code (trim + uppercase), look up the coupon, and validate order/coupon eligibility in a fixed precedence.
+- Compute the discount for FIXED and PERCENT coupons, applying the optional cap and clamping to the order amount so the final amount can never go negative.
+- Persist the order discount columns, insert a `coupon_redemptions` row, and increment `coupons.used_count` atomically in a single transaction; any failure rolls everything back.
+- Return the updated order (same shape as `GET /orders/:id`) on success.
+- Reject invalid bodies, unknown orders/coupons, non-pending/non-active/unusable coupons with the documented error codes.
+- Add tests covering the acceptance criteria.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+
+- `order-coupons`: redeeming a single coupon against a pending order via `POST /orders/:id/apply-coupon`, including normalization, eligibility rules, discount calculation, atomic persistence, and the error contract.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+<!-- none: no existing specs -->
+
+## Impact
+
+- `src/routes/orders.ts` — register the new route (parse params only).
+- `src/services/orderService.ts` — apply-coupon use case and all business rules; needs access to coupon data and repositories.
+- `src/repositories/orderRepository.ts` — update discount columns and read/write within a transaction.
+- `src/repositories/couponRepository.ts` — load coupon, insert redemption, increment `used_count`.
+- `src/app.ts` — wiring if the service needs additional collaborators.
+- `tests/` — new tests for the apply-coupon endpoint; existing tests must keep passing.
+- No schema changes, no new dependencies, no changes to existing tests.
