+# Tasks
+
+## 1. Persistence layer
+
+- [x] 1.1 Add `applyCoupon(id, couponCode, discountCents, finalAmountCents)` to `OrderRepository` that sets the three order columns; verify `npm run build` passes.
+- [x] 1.2 Add `transaction<T>(fn)` to `OrderRepository` that runs `BEGIN`/`COMMIT` and rolls back on error; verify a thrown error inside the callback leaves the row unchanged in a scratch test.
+- [x] 1.3 Add `insertRedemption(orderId, couponCode, discountCents, createdAt)` and `incrementUsedCount(code)` to `CouponRepository`; verify `npm run build` passes and inserting then reading back yields one redemption and `usedCount + 1`.
+
+## 2. Discount calculation
+
+- [x] 2.1 Add a pure `computeDiscount(coupon, amountCents)` helper returning integer cents: FIXED = value, PERCENT = `floor(amount * value / 100)`, then `min` with `maxDiscountCents` when non-null, then clamp to `amountCents`; verify with unit tests covering the SPEC discount scenarios (fixed 10000→1500, percent 10000→2000, percent 999→149, cap 100000/20/5000→5000, fixed 1000 with value 3000→1000, uncapped).
+
+## 3. Apply-coupon use case
+
+- [x] 3.1 Add `OrderService.applyCoupon(id, rawCode)` with `CouponRepository` injected and normalize the code (trim + uppercase); verify `npm run build` passes and `" save20 "` resolves `SAVE20` in a test.
+- [x] 3.2 Implement body validation (`INVALID_REQUEST`) and the order checks (`ORDER_NOT_FOUND`, `ORDER_NOT_PENDING`, `COUPON_ALREADY_APPLIED`) in the documented precedence; verify each code with an endpoint test.
+- [x] 3.3 Implement the coupon checks (`COUPON_NOT_FOUND`, `COUPON_INACTIVE`, `COUPON_NOT_YET_VALID`, `COUPON_EXPIRED`, `COUPON_USAGE_EXHAUSTED`, `MINIMUM_NOT_MET`) using `this.clock()` for `now`, with inclusive `validFrom` and exclusive `validUntil`; verify each code and both window boundaries with tests.
+- [x] 3.4 Implement the atomic write through `OrderRepository.transaction` (`applyCoupon` + `insertRedemption` + `incrementUsedCount`) and return the reloaded order; verify order fields, one redemption row, and `usedCount + 1`, and that a rejected request leaves all three unchanged.
+
+## 4. Route and wiring
+
+- [x] 4.1 Register `POST /orders/:id/apply-coupon` in `src/routes/orders.ts` (parse id, pass `couponCode` through) and inject `CouponRepository` into `OrderService` in `src/app.ts`; verify the existing suite still passes with `npm test`.
+- [x] 4.2 Verify an ordered rejection for a malformed id responds 400 `INVALID_REQUEST` and that success returns 200 with a body equal to a subsequent `GET /orders/:id`.
+
+## 5. Acceptance and integration
+
+- [x] 5.1 Add endpoint tests for AC-01 through AC-06 and AC-08 through AC-10 in a new `tests/` file, leaving the existing tests untouched; verify `npm test` passes.
+- [x] 5.2 Verify `npm run build` and `npm test` both pass end to end on a clean run.
+
+## Workflow follow-up
+
+- Archive the change after the project's review requirements are satisfied.
+- Verify the archived result.
